# Pin line endings in the repo itself: core.autocrlf is per-clone config and cannot be relied on.
# Text files are stored with LF in the index and checked out with LF on every platform (Go tooling,
# shell scripts and Dockerfiles all require LF; gofmt rewrites CRLF files, which is how a one-line
# change used to turn into a whole-file diff, e.g. internal/handler/order_handler.go).
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never touch binary files.
*.pdf binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.zip binary
*.xlsx binary
*.docx binary
*.mp4 binary
*.mp3 binary
